Create one production-ready background asset for a normal, unselected slot in
the Urkaaaz match HUD. The same asset will be reused behind unit, ammunition,
and spell choices. Do not create a screen mockup or separate category variants.

## Reference inputs

Attach:

1. The match-HUD screenshot attached to this request. Use it as the primary
   visual target for slot outline, corner shape, border weight, and contrast.
   Match the normal unit/spell/ammunition slots in the bottom dock; do not
   copy the bright selected-ammunition glow.
2. The square frame sample attached to this request only as an example of a
   self-contained square frame that can be resized proportionally. Its heavy
   border is not a style target.
3. The approved `health_card_frame.png` and
   `match_hud_dock_group_frame.png` only as secondary references for palette
   and material. Their larger, heavier panel treatments are not a target for
   this small slot.
4. The approved match-HUD redesign reference.
5. Existing unit, ammunition, and spell icons to check that the slot's center
   remains a clear backdrop for varied artwork.

Use the supplied images as visual references only. Do not reproduce their
labels, artwork, values, or complete screen.

## Output

- Filename: `match_hud_slot_frame_normal.png`
- Source path: `assets_src/match/hud/match_hud_slot_frame_normal.png`
- Canvas: exactly 256 x 256 pixels.
- Format: RGBA PNG.
- Produce exactly one standalone asset.
- Keep the source canvas square and design it to support Android
  Nine-patch/9-slice resizing to different slot widths and heights. Do not
  include Nine-patch guide pixels or markers in this source PNG.

## Design

Create a lightweight, square slot outline for a tappable HUD item. Reproduce
the screenshot's restrained, fine-edged treatment: a narrow, crisp bronze-gold
outer line, at most a very subtle muted-steel inner highlight, and a quiet,
dark translucent center. Use shallow beveling only; the slot should read as a
thin framed card, not a miniature armored panel.

Keep the border visually close to the screenshot's normal unit and spell
slots: narrow, low-profile, and subordinate to the artwork. Use small,
symmetrical clipped/chamfered corners rather than bulky rounded shoulders.
Keep the interior detail-free so the item icon drawn by Android stays dominant.
The edge must remain discernible at approximately 48 dp without becoming
thick, bright, deeply beveled, or more ornate than the screenshot.

## Nine-patch resizing

Prepare this image as a clean Nine-patch source. Keep each corner's shape and
ornament within a compact fixed area. Make the middle of every side straight
and uniform, and keep the center plain and free of directional texture. When
resized, the corners and border thickness should remain unchanged while only
the simple edge segments and quiet center stretch.

The same frame should work at square, wider, narrower, and taller dimensions.
Do not stretch, squash, crop, or tile the corner treatment. Maintain a
practical minimum size large enough to fit all four corners. The generated
PNG must not contain guide pixels; after the asset is approved, its stretch
and content regions will be marked in the Android Nine-patch resource.

This asset represents only the normal, unselected state. It must not look
selected, active, disabled, unavailable, or pressed. The selected-state asset
is generated separately; interaction feedback and accessibility state remain
dynamic UI behavior.

## Runtime content — do not bake into the image

Android renders the following dynamically above this background:

- the unit, ammunition, or spell illustration;
- item names, costs, ammunition stock, reload feedback, and spell status;
- selection, active, disabled, unavailable, pressed, or other interaction
  states.

Do not include or imply a particular item category, item identity, team,
resource value, gameplay state, or selection state. Do not bake a drop shadow
into the PNG; any shadow is provided programmatically.

## Negative requirements

- No text, numbers, labels, icons, symbols, item illustrations, category
  markers, dividers, or progress indicators.
- No gold glow, bright selected-ammunition border, checkmark, aura, or other
  selected/active treatment.
- No gray wash, low-contrast treatment, slash, lock, or other disabled-state
  treatment.
- No blue/red team coloring, crest, shield, faction emblem, or team-specific
  detail.
- No screenshot, mockup, battlefield, character, scenery, logo, watermark,
  signature, device frame, or contact sheet.
- No opaque square canvas background: pixels outside the slot
  silhouette must be fully transparent.
- No thick frame, layered heavy rim, deep bevel, raised block, bulky ornament,
  spikes, large rivets, excessive glow, neon, or busy texture that competes
  with the live icon.
- No pill-shaped corners, uneven corners, asymmetric edge, jagged contour, or
  fragile detail that disappears at the in-game display size.

## Review checklist

- Confirm the output is one valid 256 x 256 RGBA PNG with the exact filename
  and no Nine-patch guide pixels.
- Confirm the exterior is transparent and the interior remains dark and
  unobstructed behind all three item categories.
- Preview it at several widths and heights, including approximately 48 x 48
  dp, with unit, ammunition, and spell artwork; it must work consistently for
  each.
- Verify that Nine-patch resizing preserves the corners and border thickness
  and stretches only the straight edges and plain center.
- Compare the normal slot directly with the screenshot's normal unit/spell
  slots. It should look thinner and lighter than the surrounding dock panels;
  exclude the selected ammunition glow.
- Compare its restrained normal-state edge with the separate selected-state
  design; do not bake any interaction state into this asset.
- Do not integrate it into Android resources until approved.
